  {
    "slug": "tree-2",
    "date": "2026-10-29",
    "ref": "showcase/tree",
    "title": "Tree stand: optimised 0.1.0",
    "note": "Second attempt: a goblet, not a tree. With the feet together as a trunk and the load round the plate's edge, it grew a cone flaring out at 45° to the plate. The twisting case and six evenly spaced loads favour a closed shell over separate branches. In one piece, no overhangs past 45°, bridges 2.6 mm; 48 g of PLA; 266 steps in 55 min.",
    "source": "bench",
    "picture": true
  },
  {
    "slug": "tree",
    "date": "2026-10-29",
    "ref": "showcase/tree",
    "title": "Tree stand: optimised 0.1.0",
    "note": "First attempt: came out as a stool, three straight legs under a plate, not a tree. The loads sit right above the feet and the solid plate spreads them, so straight columns are stiffest. In one piece, prints standing on its feet with 3 mm bridges under the plate, 48 g of PLA; 237 steps on 40,960 cells in 49 min.",
    "source": "bench",
    "picture": true
  },
  {
    "slug": "twist-2",
    "date": "2026-10-28",
    "ref": "showcase/twist",
    "title": "Twisted tube: optimised 0.1.0",
    "note": "Second attempt, in one piece: 25% of a 40 × 80 mm cylinder with struts at least 5 mm thick. The wall opens into diamond windows running round it in a spiral. 249 steps on 23,040 cells of 2 mm in 19 min; printable standing up, 32 g of PLA.",
    "source": "bench",
    "picture": true
  },
  {
    "slug": "twist",
    "date": "2026-10-28",
    "ref": "showcase/twist",
    "title": "Twisted tube, first attempt: falls apart",
    "note": "Failed: the struts came out one cell thick, and a one-cell strut at 45° on a cube grid touches only at edges, so the part fell into 11 pieces with many thin, non-solid bits. Settings: 15% of a 40 × 80 mm cylinder, filter 3 mm on 2 mm cells. Rerun with a 5 mm filter and 25% material.",
    "source": "bench",
    "picture": true
